  "source_dataset": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE",
  "text": "Allergies:\nPatient recorded as having No Known Allergies to Drugs\n\nChief Complaint:\nHeadache, abdominal pain, and weakness\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nHistory obtained with ___ interpreter at bedside. Pt is a ___ \nyear old ___ speaking woman with a H/O of afib, HTN, \nasthma and recent ICH s/p evacuation on ___ at ___ most \nrecently admitted from rehab with HA, \nfever, confusion ___. LP showed 660 WBC and culture was \npositive for coagulase negative staph resistant to PCN, but \nsensitive to Vancomycin. She was discharged back to rehab \n(___) on IV Vanco x 3 weeks, which ended ysterday. \n\nShe now returns with c/o headaches, abdominal pain, and \nbilateral ___ weakness. In the ED an LP showed 19 WBC, 400 RBCs, \nxanthocromic and clear CSF. UA showed leukocytes. She received \nIV Cipro, ceftriaxone, and vancomycin. She was afebrile. No \nleukocytosis on CBC. Head CT w/o contrast initial reading \nnegative for acute changes. No new bleeds.\n\nBy the time she arrived to the floor, she states her headache \nhas resolved completely. She is alert and oriented x 3. She \ndenies nausea, vomiting, or neck stiffness. She was alert and \noriented. She states she has chronic epigastric pain which is \nunchanged. She denies chest pain. ROS is also positive for new \nurinary incontinance - \"leakage\", urinary urgency without \ndysuria. She denies weakness but states that she is dizzy when \nsitting up and standing. No sensory complaints. ROS: all other \nsystems negative.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\n___ old woman s/p ICH while on coumadin for A.fib is \ntransferred from ___ rehab for weakness, abd pain, HA. By \nsystem:\n\n1. Headache - Likely tension headache.  Her symptoms resolved by \nthe time she reached the floor. No evidence of meningitis. LP \nwas negative. Received IV Cipro, Ceftriaxone, and Vanco IV in \nthe ED. These were not continued. She just finshed a 3 week \ncourse of IV Vanco. CSF cultures were negative.  Head CT did not \nshow new intracranial hemorrhage.  Patient was given tylenol \nprn.\n\n2. UTI - Patient started on Cipro.  Urine cx later came back \nnegative.  She was given 3 days of antibiotics.\n\n3. Urinary incontinence - continue ditropan\n\n4. Constipation - Likely contributing to abdominal discomfort.  \nPatient given aggresive bowel regimen. Patient had no abd pain \nat discharge.\n\n5. Dyspepsia:  COntinued PPI and gave TUMS prn.  Likely \ncontributing to abd discomfort.\n\n6. Atrial Fibrillation - Rate well controlled. On Ca-channel \nblocker and beta blocker. On ASA for anticoagulation, which is \nappropriate given her history. Will need to get OK from \nneurosurgery before resuming coumadin.\n\n7. Hypertension - Continued metoprolol and diltiazem\n\n8. Code status - full.\n\n9. Dispo - Patient discharged back to ___ rehab in stable \ncondition.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nUrinary tract infection\nTension headache\nDyspepsia",
